{
  "description": "May this bill be voided now, on this counter, with this approver (POS-11, PRD W5, D-002, owner answers 1 and 2 to W1-12)? Unless a case says otherwise: bill C03-S000412 (Rs 4,320 cash due) finalized on this counter (C03, …d1) today, 2026-11-03; the cash desk says it is still pending; the approver is the manager …a2 (pos.void, window same_day_before_handover); the reason is wrong_price with no note. Staff as in testing/counter.ts. The cash desk status is what the counter knows: the live check online (pending, received, paid_out, not_applicable) or unknown. A bill without cash due needs nothing from the desk. No window allows a void after the handover (owner answer 1): same_day behaves as same_day_before_handover. The first problem, in order: other_device, already_voided, other_day, handed_over, not_permitted, window_none, reason_required, note_required, note_too_long (200). handoverSeen is what the void document records; warning desk_unknown when the desk couldn't be asked about a bill with cash. W1-23 (D-111): the bill's payments decide too: a part that brings money in is known from the desk's status (cash) or the person's answer (asked, by method; a bank, wallet or card part always), and paymentChecks records them; problems payment_unanswered, money_arrived and payment_missing come after handed_over.",
